:"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2020-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":17647.34,"currency":"USD"},"label":"one-time"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2021-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":183049,"currency":"USD"},"label":"recurring"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2021-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":71799.16,"currency":"USD"},"label":"one-time"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2022-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":162534,"currency":"USD"},"label":"recurring"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2022-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":22816.34,"currency":"USD"},"label":"one-time"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2023-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":79753,"currency":"USD"},"label":"recurring"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2023-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":26462.79,"currency":"USD"},"label":"one-time"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":74406.5,"currency":"USD"},"label":"recurring"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":363.42,"currency":"USD"},"label":"one-time"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":52868,"currency":"USD"},"label":"recurring"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":6438,"currency":"USD"},"label":"one-time"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":20253,"currency":"USD"},"label":"recurring"},{"__typename":"TimeSeriesAmountNode","date":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","amount":{"__typename":"Amount","value":4481,"currency":"USD"},"label":"one-time"}]}},"Collective:dgm9bnk8-0437xqry-ejpvzeol-jdayw5re":{"__typename":"Collective","id":"dgm9bnk8-0437xqry-ejpvzeol-jdayw5re","currency":"USD","stats":{"__ref":"AccountStats:dgm9bnk8-0437xqry-ejpvzeol-jdayw5re"}}},"__APOLLO_VARIABLES__":{"slug":"babel","nbContributorsPerContributeCard":4},"__APOLLO_ERROR__":null,"__APOLLO_QUERY_DATA__":{"Collective":{"__typename":"Collective","id":580,"idV2":"dgm9bnk8-0437xqry-ejpvzeol-jdayw5re","slug":"babel","path":"/babel","name":"Babel","hasHosting":false,"description":"Babel is the community maintained compiler for evolving the future of JavaScript","longDescription":"\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eYou'll be helping Babel's maintainers manage a project used by most of the world to compile their JavaScript (including most frameworks like React, Ember, Vue) with more than \u003ca href=\"https://opencollective.com/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.npmjs.com%2Fpackage%2F%40babel%2Fcore\"\u003e28 million downloads/week\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eThe funds are generally intended to be used to:\u003c/div\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eSupport part/full-time maintainers: most core team members contribute in their spare time, and being able to focus on work would go well with less burnout and a sustainable future for the project as a whole.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAllow us to meet in-person as well as attend conferences and \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/tc39/agendas\"\u003eTC39 (the committee that specifies JavaScript) meetings\u003c/a\u003e which are every 2 months at various companies around the world. This allows us to be involved in the process that moves various JavaScript proposals forward, allowing us to understand and take part in that discussion and be an implementer (similar to other browsers).\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eBabel helps you write the latest version of JavaScript, and is helping shape the future of the language itself. It's used at Facebook, Google, Netflix, and \u003ca href=\"https://opencollective.com/redirect?url=http%3A%2F%2Fbabeljs.io%2Fusers\"\u003ehundreds of other companies\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eWhen your target browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, IE) don't support certain features natively, it helps you compile it down to a supported version.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIn short, developers want to take advantage of the latest syntax in JavaScript before it's implemented in browsers, now. Because the version of JavaScript depends on the client's browser, we can't rely on the fact they are using an up to date browser.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eBabel abstracts the browser away so that you can worry about writing your application rather than trying to figure out what features are supported in each one.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","backgroundImage":"https://cl.ly/3A1a2M0F430p/babel-compressed.jpg","backgroundImageUrl":"https://images.opencollective.com/babel/9a38a01/background.jpg","twitterHandle":"babeljs","repositoryUrl":"https://github.com/babel","website":"https://babeljs.io","socialLinks":[{"__typename":"SocialLink","type":"WEBSITE","url":"https://babeljs.io"},{"__typename":"SocialLink","type":"TWITTER","url":"https://twitter.com/babeljs"},{"__typename":"SocialLink","type":"GITHUB","url":"https://github.com/babel"}],"location":{"__typename":"LocationType","id":"48715","country":null},"tags":["javascript","es6","es2015","babel","compiler","open source"],"company":null,"type":"COLLECTIVE","currency":"USD","createdAt":"Sat Apr 01 2017 14:02:10 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","settings":{"goals":[{"key":"8d8bddbd-a9e0-472a-a9c4-0c1786f927ab","type":"yearlyBudget","title":"3 maintainers","amount":33333300,"description":"The goal is to pay Henry, Jùnliàng and Nicolò a salary as maintainers."}],"editor":"html","features":{"recurringExpenses":true},"githubOrg":"babel","moderation":{"rejectedCategories":[]},"collectivePage":{"sections":[{"name":"goals","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"CONTRIBUTE","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"contribute","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true},{"name":"events","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"connected-collectives","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"top-financial-contributors","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true},{"name":"contributors","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true},{"name":"projects","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true}]},{"name":"CONTRIBUTIONS","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"recurring-contributions","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true}]},{"name":"BUDGET","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"budget","type":"SECTION","version":2,"isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]}]},{"name":"CONNECT","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"updates","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"conversations","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":[]}]},{"name":"ABOUT","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"about","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true},{"name":"our-team","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true}]}],"showGoals":false,"background":{"crop":{"x":-1091,"y":-523},"zoom":0.5},"primaryColor":"#297EFF"},"goalsInterpolation":"auto","forceNewPaypalPayments":true,"disablePublicExpenseSubmission":true},"isActive":true,"isApproved":true,"isVerified":false,"isArchived":false,"isFrozen":false,"isSuspended":false,"isHost":false,"isIncognito":false,"isGuest":false,"isTrustedHost":false,"isFirstPartyHost":false,"hostFeePercent":10,"platformFeePercent":0,"platformContributionAvailable":true,"image":"https://opencollective-production.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/8ef2d0e0-16e1-11e7-9b5a-89d03aeb3ad4.png","imageUrl":"https://images.opencollective.com/babel/3787879/logo/256.png","canApply":false,"canContact":true,"supportedExpenseTypes":["INVOICE","RECEIPT"],"features":{"__typename":"CollectiveFeatures","id":"dgm9bnk8-0437xqry-ejpvzeol-jdayw5re","ABOUT":"ACTIVE","CONNECTED_ACCOUNTS":"AVAILABLE","RECEIVE_FINANCIAL_CONTRIBUTIONS":"ACTIVE","RECURRING_CONTRIBUTIONS":"AVAILABLE","EVENTS":"AVAILABLE","PROJECTS":"AVAILABLE","USE_EXPENSES":"ACTIVE","RECEIVE_EXPENSES":"ACTIVE","FUNDS_GRANTS_MANAGEMENT":"DISABLED","COLLECTIVE_GOALS":"DISABLED","TOP_FINANCIAL_CONTRIBUTORS":"ACTIVE","CONVERSATIONS":"ACTIVE","UPDATES":"AVAILABLE","TEAM":"ACTIVE","CONTACT_FORM":"ACTIVE","RECEIVE_HOST_APPLICATIONS":"UNSUPPORTED","HOST_DASHBOARD":"UNSUPPORTED","TRANSACTIONS":"ACTIVE","PUBLIC_PROFILE":"ACTIVE"},"memberOf":[{"__typename":"Member","id":42587}],"stats":{"__typename":"CollectiveStatsType","id":580,"balance":19684687,"yearlyBudget":25710999,"backers":{"__typename":"BackersStatsType","id":580,"all":1258,"users":1010,"organizations":227}},"connectedTo":[],"parentCollective":null,"host":{"__typename":"Organization","id":11004,"name":"Open Source Collective","slug":"opensource","type":"ORGANIZATION","hasHosting":true,"location":{"__typename":"LocationType","id":"288932","country":"US"},"settings":{"kyc":{"skipRequestIntroduction":true},"tos":"https://docs.google.com/document/u/1/d/e/2PACX-1vQbiyK2Fe0jLdh4vb9BfHY4bJ1LCo4Qvy0jg9P29ZkiC8y_vKJ_1fNgIbV0p6UdvbcT8Ql1gVto8bf9/pub","beta":{"embedContributionFlow":true},"apply":true,"goals":[{}],"budget":{"version":"v2"},"editor":"html","invoice":{"templates":{"default":{"info":"EIN 82-2037583\n\nThis payment is not deductible as a charitable contribution for U.S. federal income tax purposes.\n\nIf you have any need for a refund, please see our refund policy (below) and send an email to hello@oscollective.org\nhttps://docs.oscollective.org/for-donors-companies-organizations-and-individuals/refund-requests#refund-requests","title":""}},"expenseTemplates":{"default":{}}},"features":{"privacyVcc":true,"hostVendors":true,"transferwise":true,"virtualCards":true,"paypalPayouts":true,"stripePaymentIntent":true,"multiCurrencyExpenses":true},"feesOnTop":true,"moderation":{"rejectedCategories":[]},"earlyAccess":{"activityLog":true},"applyMessage":"If you can't authenticate using \u003e100 GitHub stars, please explain how you meet the alternative criteria: https://www.oscollective.org/#criteria","expenseTypes":{"GRANT":false,"INVOICE":true,"RECEIPT":true},"transferwise":{"ott":false,"transferDetails":true},"virtualcards":{"policy":"\u003cdiv\u003eVirtual cards are debit card numbers issued to OSC's hosted collectives for paying online expenses like recurring vendor payments, online resources or tools, and subscriptions. They are tied directly to a collective's budget on the Open Collective platform.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHOW IT WORKS\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eFunds are spent only as transactions occur. (Setting up a card does not remove any money from your initiative's budget.)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSubmit a virtual card request with the intended use of the card \u003cstrong\u003e(please specify the names of the services you will use) \u003c/strong\u003eand the amount budgeted for that use monthly \u003cstrong\u003e(e.g. $300/month)\u003c/strong\u003e. We will review your request and reply with any questions.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eIf your collective needs a higher limit on your virtual card please request a limit increase by contacting us at hello@oscollective.org\u003cstrong\u003e \u003c/strong\u003ewith the intended use and the amount increase needed.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eTo receive an increase, the project must have a budget on their Open Collective account that exceeds the corresponding amount and must demonstrate that a higher limit is necessary.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eCards must be used in compliance with our policy below.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eELIGIBILITY\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOSC reviews each virtual card request individually. When determining eligibility, we consider:\u003c/div\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eHow long the project has been hosted by OSC\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhether the project is in good standing with OSC\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe requesting admin’s history with OSC\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe project’s available balance and transaction history\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe project's typical incoming contributions and outgoing expenses\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe anticipated monthly spending amount\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe proposed use of the card\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eREQUIREMENTS/POLICY\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThese are \u003cstrong\u003evirtual cards. \u003c/strong\u003eNo physical card will be issued, so these cannot be used in-store.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAll transactions should comply with normal usage of initiative funds as outlined in our \u003ca href=\"https://app.gitbook.com/o/-LWSZizNMEjL8_DrMNdF/s/-M9Neg20-zKzu0MhF2d2/getting-started/terms\"\u003eTerms of Fiscal Sponsorship\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eIf a card has not been used for more than 15 months, the card will be frozen\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAdmins requesting a card must have their legal name and address on file on their individual Open Collective user profile (not the collective's profile). Only the display name is public; legal name and address are visible only to OSC as fiscal host.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eIf no receipt has been uploaded to an expense after 30 days, the card will be frozen\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e​Admins are personally liable for misuse\u0026nbsp;\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eVirtual cards \u003cstrong\u003emay not \u003c/strong\u003ebe used for \u003ca href=\"https://app.gitbook.com/o/-LWSZizNMEjL8_DrMNdF/s/-M9Neg20-zKzu0MhF2d2/how-it-works/payouts\"\u003epaying/reimbursing people\u003c/a\u003e, that should be done on the OC platform.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eREQUESTING A CARD\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eOnly project admin's can request a card. \u003cstrong\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLog in to the Open Collective platform. In the left navigation, click on Virtual Cards -\u0026gt; Request a Card\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOSC will assign the card (please allow time for processing)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOnce assigned, the card assignee will be notified via email and the card's details will appear in the initiative's Settings for you to use (in accordance with this policy)\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCARDHOLDER CONTACT DETAILS:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf you need to input Cardholder contact details/address:\u003c/div\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eName\u003c/strong\u003e: Open Source Collective\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAddress\u003c/strong\u003e: 440 N Barranca Ave #3939 Covina, CA 91723, USA\u0026nbsp;\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAFTER A PURCHASE IS MADE\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eFunds are withdrawn from your initiative immediately.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAn \"Invitation to submit an expense\" will be sent to your initiative admins\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAdmins will be asked to submit your receipt\u0026nbsp;\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf the receipt is not submitted within 30 days, the card access will be paused until you do submit the receipt\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","reminder":true,"autopause":true,"requestcard":true,"autopauseUnusedCards":{"period":455,"enabled":true}},"cryptoEnabled":false,"collectivePage":{"sections":[{"name":"CONTRIBUTIONS","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"contributions","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":null},{"name":"recurring-contributions","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":[]}],"isEnabled":true},{"name":"ABOUT","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"about","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":null},{"name":"our-team","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":null}],"isEnabled":true},{"name":"CONTRIBUTE","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"contribute","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"top-financial-contributors","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true},{"name":"connected-collectives","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":false},{"name":"events","type":"SECTION","version":1,"isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"contributors","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true},{"name":"projects","type":"SECTION","version":1,"isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]}],"isEnabled":true},{"name":"CONNECT","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"updates","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"conversations","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":null}],"isEnabled":true},{"name":"BUDGET","type":"CATEGORY","sections":[{"name":"budget","type":"SECTION","version":2,"isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]},{"name":"transactions","type":"SECTION","isEnabled":true}],"isEnabled":true}],"showGoals":false,"tiersOrder":["custom",118,119,15445],"primaryColor":"#663299","useNewSections":true,"legacySectionsBackup":[{"section":"about","isEnabled":true},{"section":"contributions","isEnabled":true},{"section":"contributors","isEnabled":true},{"section":"updates","isEnabled":false},{"section":"conversations","isEnabled":false},{"section":"transactions","isEnabled":true},{"section":"recurring-contributions","isEnabled":false,"restrictedTo":[]},{"section":"contribute","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]},{"section":"budget","isEnabled":true,"restrictedTo":[]}]},"hostCollective":{"id":11004},"paymentMethods":{"manual":{"title":"Bank Transfer (manual)","legacy":true,"features":{"recurring":false},"instructions":"Note: the instructions for transfers differ depending on whether you're sending from a US or non-US bank.\n\nMake sure to include the reference number, Invoice #, or project receiving the funds in the memo field.\n\nIf you have any questions or need an Invoice, please get in touch with us at hello@oscollective.org\n\n-------------------------------------\n\nFor US transfers (ACH or Wire)\n\nAmount: {amount}\nReference: {reference}\n\nAccount Number: 202525828483\nABA / Routing: 091311229\nSWIFT: CHFGUS44021\n\nAccount type: Business Checking\nBank name: Choice Financial Group\nBank address: 4501 23rd Avenue S, Fargo, ND 58104, USA\n\nAccount name: Open Source Collective\nRecipient Address: 440 N Barranca Ave #3939 Covina, CA 91723, USA\n\n-------------------------------------\n\nInternational Bank Transfers (Wire)\nFor non-U.S. banks\n\nAmount: {amount}\nReference: {reference}\n\nRouting / Wire Number: 123205054\nSWIFT / BIC: UMPQUS6P\n\nAccount type: Business Checking\nBank Name: Columbia Bank\nBank Address: 450 Sansome St., Suite 120, San Francisco, CA 94111, United States\n\nAccount Name: Open Source Collective\nRecipient Address: 440 N Barranca Ave #3939 Covina, CA 91723, USA\n\n-------------------------------------\n\nPlease note that it will take 3~5 business days to process your payment. If you don't see your contribution within a week, please contact us at hello@oscollective.org. \n\nNOTE: WE DO NOT ACCEPT CHECKS"}},"payoutsTwoFactorAuth":{"enabled":true,"rollingLimit":1000000},"newPlatformTipsLedger":true,"forceNewPaypalPayments":true,"disableCryptoContributions":false,"exportedTransactionsFieldSets":{"yptc":{"name":"YPTC","fields":["effectiveDate","legacyId","description","type","kind","group","netAmount","currency","isRefund","isRefunded","refundLegacyId","accountSlug","accountName","oppositeAccountSlug","oppositeAccountName","paymentMethodService","paymentMethodType","orderMemo","expenseType","payoutMethodType","accountingCategoryCode","accountingCategoryN